# Agentic Code Review

Use this skill before claiming any material code-affecting task is complete, fixed, PR-ready, or merge-ready.

This is an independent review gate for agent-generated code. It combines deterministic, language-agnostic scans with one mandatory independent subagent/reviewer pass so routine work does not need several review agents by default.

The deterministic collector is tool support for the reviewer. It is not the gate by itself. A run with `0` scanner findings, `0` checkpoints, or only satisfied runtime requirements means "deterministic packet is clean"; it does not mean the agentic-code-review gate is complete until a subagent/reviewer has independently reviewed the packet and evidence, unless the change is truly trivial, subagent/task tooling is concretely unavailable after an attempt, or the user explicitly disables independent review for this task.

Hard rule: material code-affecting work that triggers this skill MUST use one independent reviewer subagent together with the collector packet unless the change is truly trivial, subagent/task tooling is concretely unavailable after an attempt, or the user explicitly disables independent review for this task. In Codex, use an appropriate independent reviewer role such as `reviewer`, `security-reviewer`, `api-designer`, `architect`, `performance-reviewer`, or another risk-matched reviewer. In OpenCode or Claude, use the native task/subagent equivalent. The implementing agent must not approve its own work.

Standing reviewer authorization: the global harness authorizes exactly one independent reviewer subagent/task for this gate on material code-affecting work. Do not skip that reviewer by citing missing user authorization when the current task, plan, or harness instructions require `agentic-code-review`. This authorization does not cover extra reviewers, builder agents, QA agents, parallel implementation agents, or specialist escalations beyond the one risk-matched reviewer. If the runtime/tool still blocks subagent/task use after a concrete attempt, report the concrete blocker and mark the full gate incomplete.

