## Trigger

Run this skill for material changes to:

- executable code, tests, contracts, database access, migrations, CI/CD, package manifests, lockfiles, runtime behavior, or user-facing behavior;
- bug fixes, refactors, generated code, or review-feedback fixes;
- any implementation where correctness, maintainability, scale, or regression risk matters.

Skip only for trivial non-code edits, formatting-only changes, factual answers, concrete subagent/task unavailability after an attempt, or explicit user disablement of independent review for this task. When skipped, state why the gate was not useful or why the full gate could not run.

## Gate Workflow

1. Re-read the user request, active plan, review feedback, and changed diff.
2. Run the deterministic collector from a repository root when a repository is available:
   ```bash
   node ~/.agents/skills/agentic-code-review/scripts/collect-review-context.mjs
   ```
3. For cross-repo work, pass explicit roots:
   ```bash
   node ~/.agents/skills/agentic-code-review/scripts/collect-review-context.mjs --root ../repo-a --root ../repo-b
   ```
4. For committed PR-ready branches, historical PRs, or already-merged code, pin the comparison as needed:
   ```bash
   node ~/.agents/skills/agentic-code-review/scripts/collect-review-context.mjs --base origin/main
   node ~/.agents/skills/agentic-code-review/scripts/collect-review-context.mjs --base <base-sha> --head <head-sha>
   node ~/.agents/skills/agentic-code-review/scripts/collect-review-context.mjs --full-repo
   ```
   `--full-repo` also supports a plain directory that is not a Git repository; in that mode it walks files under the selected root with the collector's normal generated/local artifact ignores.
5. When scanning this skill itself, rely on the built-in self-scan defaults so intentional smoke fixtures and detector-rule implementation strings do not dominate the packet.
6. For CI, dashboards, calibration, or machine-readable packets, use:
   ```bash
   node ~/.agents/skills/agentic-code-review/scripts/collect-review-context.mjs --base origin/main --json
   ```
7. For project-specific tuning, use `.agentic-reviewrc.json` at the repository root or pass:
   ```bash
   node ~/.agents/skills/agentic-code-review/scripts/collect-review-context.mjs --config .agentic-reviewrc.json
   ```
8. Inventory optional external tools without running them by default. Run installed external tools only after scoped approval and only when the task benefits:
   ```bash
   node ~/.agents/skills/agentic-code-review/scripts/collect-review-context.mjs --run-external-tools
   node ~/.agents/skills/agentic-code-review/scripts/collect-review-context.mjs --run-external-tools --external-tool jscpd
   node ~/.agents/skills/agentic-code-review/scripts/collect-review-context.mjs --run-external-tools --allow-tool-downloads
   ```
   Use `templates/deep-review-toolbelt-2026.json` as the optional tool manifest.
9. Treat the collector output as a review packet, not as a pass/fail gate. A clean packet may reduce reviewer scope; it must not replace independent review for material code-affecting work.
10. Inspect the packet and run additional focused checks or probes when it flags material risk.
11. Satisfy applicable runtime verification requirements with real production code path execution, or state the blocker, substitute verification, and residual uncertainty.
12. Resolve any user input checkpoints whose answer can change whether an item is blocking.
13. Send one independent reviewer subagent the packet, objective, diff, files touched, verification evidence, answered checkpoints, and known skipped checks.
14. Fix every blocking finding or explicitly report why it is not actionable.
15. Re-run targeted verification after fixes.
16. Only then make completion, PR-ready, or merge-ready claims.

Invalid closeout examples:

- "The agentic-code-review gate passed because `collect-review-context.mjs` returned 0 findings."
- "The gate is complete because tests, lint, typecheck, build, and `git diff --check` passed."
- "No independent reviewer subagent was run, but the deterministic scan was clean."

Correct closeout wording when independent review has not run:

- "The deterministic agentic-code-review packet is clean, but the full agentic-code-review gate is incomplete because an independent reviewer subagent has not run."

Valid skip reasons are limited to truly trivial changes with explicit rationale, subagent/task tooling technically unavailable after a concrete attempt, or the user explicitly disabling independent review for that task.

## Definition Of Done Checklist

Before the reviewer pass is considered ready, assemble this checklist for the packet or final handoff:

- Diff is minimal, scoped, and reviewable.
- Contracts, schemas, docs, migrations, or changelog were updated when the touched behavior requires it.
- The exact touched production code path was exercised, or the blocker, substitute verification, and residual uncertainty are stated.
- Focused tests cover the changed behavior and at least one meaningful negative, empty, invalid, permission, or edge path when the behavior can fail.
- UI/browser changes include the QA evidence contract: flow, initial state, actions, observed result, screenshot/video when applicable, and bugs found or `No bug observed.`
- Validation summary is behavior-oriented; raw command dumps are not used as reviewer-facing proof.
- Lint/format, typecheck/build, lockfile/package-manager checks, screenshots, and PR metadata were run or explicitly classified as not relevant.
- Agentic-code-review deterministic packet was generated and interpreted as evidence, not as approval.
- One independent reviewer subagent completed the agentic review, or the change was trivial and the skip reason is explicit.
- Specialist escalation was considered and used only when a concrete trigger applies.
- Skipped checks include exact reason and residual risk.
- If a PR is open or being opened, PR body validation text summarizes tests by behavior and risk protected, not command history.

## Fixture Smoke Test

After editing this skill or its scripts, run:

```bash
node ~/.agents/skills/agentic-code-review/scripts/smoke-review-toolbelt.mjs
```

The smoke creates temporary repositories and verifies core gates, including full-repo snapshot scans, local artifact ignores, plain-directory scans, self-scan defaults, symlink/path escape protections, public skill contract text, and quality-gate ratchet generation.

For a fast no-dependency package check before the full smoke, run:

```bash
node ~/.agents/skills/agentic-code-review/scripts/validate-skill-package.mjs
```

This validator protects skill performance by enforcing frontmatter, reference routing, public-corpus size budgets, support-file references, local-path hygiene, and smoke coverage of the public contract.

## CI Quality Gate Ratchet Workflow

When creating or standardizing CI quality gates, load `references/quality-gate-ratchet.md` and generate a repository-specific ratchet instead of copying a generic workflow. The generated workflow must be reviewed against current GitHub Actions docs for triggers, least-privilege `GITHUB_TOKEN` permissions, untrusted context handling, dependency caching, concurrency, and artifacts.

```bash
node ~/.agents/skills/agentic-code-review/scripts/generate-quality-gate-ratchet.mjs --root . --base origin/main --write
```

Review generated files before committing, then run:

```bash
node docs/ai/quality-gate/check-ratchet.mjs
```

